meta {
  name: Change Status To Tiered Pricing
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/?alondra-webhook=change_status_to_tiered_pricing&id=1&status=publish
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  id: 1
  status: publish
}

docs {
  Directly UPDATEs the `status` column of one wp_alondra_tiered_pricing row by id, then
  flushes the cache. Bypasses the plugin's own REST validation entirely.

  Params (query, both required):
  - id: tiered pricing row id (int)
  - status: new status string - the plugin's List_Table expects publish, draft or trash

  Throws a 500 if no row matches `id` (id=1 only exists after Create Sample Tiered Pricing
  or Clear Data have run, since Clear Data resets AUTO_INCREMENT to 1).
}
